{% set local_problem %}
<p>Monrovia homes face two common gutter problems. Older homes often have sectional gutters that leak at every joint after years of expansion and contraction. Newer homes frequently have builder-grade gutters — the cheapest option that meets code — that overflow during heavy rain and may already be showing wear.</p>

<p>Both situations lead to the same result: water going where it shouldn't. Overflow damages fascia boards, erodes landscaping, and can threaten foundations — especially on Monrovia's clay soil that doesn't absorb water well.</p>

<p>Seamless gutters solve these problems. Custom fabrication means gutters that fit perfectly. No seams means no leaks. And proper sizing means gutters that can actually handle North Alabama's 55+ inches of annual rainfall.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Seamless gutters are continuous gutters with no joints except at corners and downspouts. We bring our portable gutter machine to your Monrovia home and fabricate each run to the exact length needed — right in your driveway.</p>

<p>This custom approach eliminates the weak points where sectional gutters fail. No seams means no leaks and fewer places for debris to accumulate. The result is better performance, better appearance, and dramatically longer lifespan.</p>
{% endset %}

